Found by mcp-hub-binary-worker during k44. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-03-forked-class-workers-design.md, "The packed binary", says a worker's lazy require reads the PAR archive through its reopened fds. With PAR 1.021 the whole archive is unpacked into PAR_TEMP/inc on first start and require reads from there; a member read reopens the binary by name. Also: the hub's first fork() of any kind moves fd 5 once (PerlIO flush of PAR's bootstrap handle), so "offset unmoved" holds only from the fork onward. Correct the section (the k44 smoke now checks the real behaviour).

